# Session UI, Preview, and Changes Panel

## 1. Define behavior and data requirements

[ ] Document the right-panel states: hidden, unavailable, loading, preview, and changes
[ ] Define when a session is considered sandbox-enabled/running and what happens when the sandbox stops
[ ] Define the session status model: created time, sandbox status, streaming status, and error state
[ ] Decide which state belongs in Convex/server data and which state belongs in client UI state

## 2. Establish client state management

[ ] Add Zustand for shared UI state only (active right-panel tab, open/collapsed state, selected session)
[ ] Keep server/session state sourced from Convex instead of duplicating it in Zustand
[ ] Add typed actions/selectors and reset state when switching sessions
[ ] Handle loading, stale, disconnected, and error states without showing misleading status

## 3. Clean up the navigation

[ ] Remove the Archive button from the navbar
[ ] Add a right-panel toggle button at the end of the navbar
[ ] Make the toggle button reflect whether the panel is open or collapsed
[ ] Add an accessible label, tooltip, keyboard support, and visible focus state to the toggle
[ ] Ensure the navbar remains usable at narrow widths after the changes

## 4. Build the right-panel shell

[ ] Show the right panel only for sessions with a running/available sandbox
[ ] Define the empty state when no sandbox is available
[ ] Add open, collapsed, and restored states without losing the selected tab
[ ] Make the panel responsive and prevent it from covering core session controls
[ ] Preserve panel state across refreshes where appropriate

## 5. Implement Preview and Changes tabs

[ ] Make Preview and Changes separate tabs in the right panel
[ ] Add active-tab styling and accessible tab semantics
[ ] Keep tab content mounted or preserve its state when switching tabs where useful
[ ] Add loading, empty, and error states for both tabs
[ ] Disable or explain unavailable tabs when the sandbox is not ready

## 6. Complete the Preview panel

[ ] Render the sandbox preview in the panel
[ ] Add preview loading and connection states
[ ] Show a useful error state with retry/reconnect action
[ ] Add refresh/reload preview action
[ ] Handle preview URL changes and sandbox restarts safely
[ ] Add fullscreen/open-in-new-tab action if supported

## 7. Implement the Changes panel

[ ] Define the changes data shape and update behavior
[ ] Render changed files with clear added, modified, and deleted states
[ ] Add file selection and a readable diff view
[ ] Add loading, no-changes, and error states
[ ] Keep changes synchronized with the active sandbox/session

## 8. Improve session status visibility

[ ] Show created time in the session status area
[ ] Show sandbox status with clear labels and visual indicators
[ ] Show streaming status and distinguish active, paused, complete, and failed states
[ ] Add precise status text/tooltips instead of relying on color alone
[ ] Update statuses in real time and handle reconnects gracefully

## 9. UX polish and validation

[ ] Add consistent spacing, sizing, borders, and empty-state styling across the panel
[ ] Add transition/animation for opening and collapsing the panel without blocking interaction
[ ] Verify keyboard navigation for navbar, toggle, tabs, preview, and changes
[ ] Verify responsive behavior on desktop and narrow viewport sizes
[ ] Test session switching, sandbox start/stop, reconnects, and preview failures
[ ] Test that panel state and tab state do not leak between sessions
[ ] Run lint, typecheck, and relevant frontend tests
[ ] Use agent-browser to perform a final end-to-end UI smoke test
